        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "import",
          "nodeId": "import-template-view"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "html",
          "value": "<div style='box-sizing:border-box;width:100%;height:100%;padding:28px;background:#ffffff;font-family:system-ui;color:#0f172a;overflow:auto'><h1 style='margin:0 0 12px;font:800 24px/1.2 system-ui'>Bridge: the import half</h1><p style='margin:0 0 12px;max-width:62ch;font:400 15px/1.6 system-ui;color:#334155'><code>data.bridge.subscriptions</code> below names the exact remote event -- <code>export-template-event-source:widget.ready</code> in <a href='github://mikemartinez1974/public/templates/bridge-template/export/root.node'>bridge-template/export</a> -- and the local Event Handler that should fire when it does. The handler then invokes a local Method, same as the export side's own Method raises the event in the first place. See the export side's detail view for how auto-loading and its background-focus fix work; that explanation isn't duplicated here, since it's about the pair, not this half specifically.</p></div>"
        }
      }
